WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.158
It's just a lot of very exciting
AI features that we already

00:00:04.158 --> 00:00:07.830
infused into Microsoft
products like Office 365.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:12.595
But at Microsoft we also want
to make sure that we can offer

00:00:12.595 --> 00:00:16.360
this kind of incredible AI
experiences to our partners and

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:17.690
developers.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:21.250
How can we help them to
build just as exciting

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:22.277
AI applications?

00:00:22.277 --> 00:00:27.070
I've talked earlier about AI
platforms and other things.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:31.080
I also want to mention that
in a key to making greater AI

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.032
apps is the data.

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:36.760
That's where actually Microsoft
is in a unique position to

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.440
offer our partners, developers,
and the partners to help them to

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:46.290
build AI applications by
providing them Microsoft Graphs.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.810
It includes an word knowledge
graph like what you can get from

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:51.690
Bing and LinkedIn, and

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:56.580
also work knowledge graph
from Office 365 Dynamics.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.690
Now imagine that all our
customers and partners,

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:05.383
they can combine
Microsoft Graphs with their own

00:01:05.383 --> 00:01:10.940
business data and knowledge
about their own users to view

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.490
the incredible AI applications
for their customers, for

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:17.920
the employees, and
for their business.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:21.150
So we feel very, very excited
about the opportunities there

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:22.728
that we can work together.

00:01:22.728 --> 00:01:26.860
And one particularly unique
thing about Microsoft is that

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.350
we have worked long and

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:32.570
hard to bring many of
these graphs together,

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:38.480
contained within a compliance
boundary that actually conforms

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:42.280
to our privacy compliance and
also data policies.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:45.454
That's very,
very important to enterprises.

00:01:45.454 --> 00:01:48.710
So those investments really
underscore what we have

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:51.448
been doing in Microsoft AI
in the research,

00:01:51.448 --> 00:01:55.150
those five things actually
I talked to you today.

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:57.830
I just want to finish
my presentation by

00:01:57.830 --> 00:02:01.200
mentioning some
also important and

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:06.020
exciting topics nowadays as
people talk about AI development

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:09.400
in partnership in society and
also in ethics.

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:13.400
So as we embrace
this AI frontier

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:19.750
we have to acknowledge that you
know concerns about AI do exist.

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:23.510
And it's actually important that
we have some universal design

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:28.650
principles and values that
help guide our thinking,

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.170
our design, and development.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:34.259
At Microsoft,
we take an ethical approach to

00:02:34.259 --> 00:02:38.800
AI design sincerely and
seriously.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:41.650
Our principle approach is
actually very critical.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:43.840
We do these things
thoughtfully and

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:49.210
in a trustworthy way both inside
the Microsoft and also outside.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:54.630
For example,
internally we have organized

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:58.090
an advisory committee
that helps ensure

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:02.170
the hereins of this principles
in our own AI development.

00:03:03.442 --> 00:03:07.288
And externally, we recognize
that we cannot do that alone.

00:03:07.288 --> 00:03:13.220
So we co-founded the Partnership
on AI just over a year ago.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:18.050
This is actually a nonprofit
organization where you see many

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:23.130
leading tech companies and
academia, civil societies, and

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:26.160
many, many nonprofit
organizations,

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:30.070
who actually care about
the future of AI development.

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:34.550
So this is actually set up
to study, formulate, and

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:38.780
share the best practices on
AI technology for all of us.

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:44.420
So we also believe that we need
to give back as we develop AI.

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:48.860
So I'd like to take this
opportunity to thank iNaturalist

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:53.440
who is the great partner in
our AI for Earth program.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:54.600
They are here today.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.660
I encourage you to stop by
their booths to talk to them,

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.380
what they do for our society.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:05.850
And finally, I would say, as the
first generation to live with

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:10.290
AI, we play a very unique
role in shaping the future.

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:15.100
As we will do so,
that is actually thoughtful.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.710
That is really our number
one focus in Microsoft.

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:23.640
So there's a lot we don't really
know about the AIC impact yet.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:27.850
But we do know is that AI
has a lot of potential

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:30.210
to really improve lives.

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.250
And it's already happening now.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:36.447
So let me share a story with you
about how AI has given voices to

00:04:36.447 --> 00:04:39.337
those who otherwise
would have had none.

00:04:39.337 --> 00:04:43.635
[MUSIC]

00:04:43.635 --> 00:04:47.199
&gt;&gt; SwiftKey Symbols is a
communication app for people who

00:04:47.199 --> 00:04:51.318
are nonverbal and it supports
them in expressing themselves.

00:04:51.318 --> 00:04:54.115
&gt;&gt; Merlin, my youngest brother,
has low functioning autism.

00:04:54.115 --> 00:04:56.158
He finds it difficult
to communicate and

00:04:56.158 --> 00:04:59.250
can get very upset if he can't
make himself understood.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:02.380
I took what we used at home with
some symbols that my mom would

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:05.850
print out, laminate, cut out and
stick velcro on, put them into

00:05:05.850 --> 00:05:08.470
folders and I just thought
I could make that easier.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:09.300
If we did it on an app,

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:12.190
be more fun for Rowan
because he loves technology.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:15.700
&gt;&gt; The underlying AI technology
which SwiftKey symbols uses,

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:18.680
is the same technology which
powers the SwiftKey keyboards.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:21.300
We use AI technology to be
able to learn from the user's

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:24.380
behavior, to see what they
like to use in terms of

00:05:24.380 --> 00:05:27.479
their own style of language, to
predict what's gonna come next.

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:32.190
&gt;&gt; It works by having a library
of symbols that you can pick and

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:33.360
choose to build your sentence.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.430
And each symbol has a word
associated with it.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.118
And we use Swift Key AI
predictive technology to learn

00:05:38.118 --> 00:05:41.524
what you've used previously,
sentences that you've previously

00:05:41.524 --> 00:05:44.510
built and then we surface what
word you might want next, and

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:47.459
what symbol you might want next,
to build your sentence.

00:05:47.459 --> 00:05:48.996
&gt;&gt; I want cheese please, Kate.

00:05:48.996 --> 00:05:51.320
&gt;&gt; Ahh, wow!

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:53.730
&gt;&gt; We developed it
alongside Riverside School,

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:56.270
which is a school specializing
in learning difficulties.

00:05:56.270 --> 00:06:00.300
&gt;&gt; To be able to express what
they want without prompting,

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:01.840
is a really big thing.

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:09.570
&gt;&gt; We have so many pupils
who are nonverbal but

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:11.040
still have so much to say.

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:15.280
&gt;&gt; I think AI can just make
everything in life more

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:18.340
efficient, so
you can enjoy life to the max.

00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:21.300
&gt;&gt; There's no better feeling
than to hear a child say

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:23.210
something that they've
wanted to say,

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:26.160
and the look on their face after
they've been able to say it.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:29.350
You can't really beat that,
because that's them expressing

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:31.910
themselves, and that's really
what you want from them.

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:33.020
&gt;&gt; It's joyous.

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:35.040
I don't think I can think
of a better word for it.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.219
It's complete joy and
celebration.

00:06:37.219 --> 00:06:40.623
[MUSIC]

00:06:40.623 --> 00:06:42.565
&gt;&gt; Well done, Tyree.

00:06:42.565 --> 00:06:47.660
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; It's really an incredible

00:06:47.660 --> 00:06:52.730
time working on AI and to use AI
to improve our human ingenuity.

00:06:52.730 --> 00:06:53.840
&gt;&gt; And we're very excited

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:56.020
to work on those
things at Microsoft.

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:58.400
Thank you very much again for
joining us today.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.760
Please, if you have time,
hang on here,

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:02.340
check out all the booths.

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:03.080
Thank you very much.

